menu "CPE SMS Forwarding Configuration"

    config CPE_SMS_MQTT_ENABLE
        bool "Forward SMS to an MQTT broker over TLS"
        depends on CPE_SMS_ENABLE
        default y
        help
            Adds a forwarding panel to the SMS page: received messages are
            published to the broker configured there, and downlink send
            commands are executed when that switch is on. Such a command may
            address any number, so the broker ACL is the only restriction on
            who is allowed to publish one. The connection is
            TLS only (mqtts://), verified against the built-in public CA
            bundle, or against a CA certificate uploaded from the panel when
            one is installed. Runs only while the WAN link is online, and an
            unreachable broker never blocks the data path.

endmenu
